cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Who Holds Government Debt? — Replication package"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the paper (preferred-citation
  below) and this replication package using the metadata in this file.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-08"
authors:
  - given-names: Yiran Emma
    family-names: Ma
    affiliation: Johns Hopkins University
repository-code: "https://github.com/emma0502/emma0502606"
abstract: >-
  Replication package for the paper "Who Holds Government Debt?". The
  paper develops a cost-minimising model of sovereign debt allocation
  in which a given stock of public debt is split across three creditor
  sectors -- domestic non-banks (with country-specific structural
  capacity), foreigners (with a uniform no-default ceiling), and the
  domestic banking system (with a convex welfare cost) -- and
  empirically estimates a high-debt banking-takeover threshold using
  the Arslanalp-Tsuda sovereign-debt-by-holder panel.
keywords:
  - sovereign debt
  - debt composition
  - financial repression
  - borrowing limits
  - REMARK
  - Reproduction
license: Apache-2.0
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Who Holds Government Debt?"
  authors:
    - given-names: Yiran Emma
      family-names: Ma
      affiliation: Johns Hopkins University
  year: 2026
  status: "in-preparation"
  abstract: >-
    Develops a cost-minimising model of sovereign debt allocation across
    domestic non-banks, foreigners, and the domestic banking system, and
    estimates a banking-takeover threshold around D = 100% of GDP using
    a cross-country panel of debt by holder.
